From b11825029bcfc8cf4d58bb47d57452e6967eb11b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Bastari Thamrin <thamrinjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:25:25 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] scx_lavd: Don't drop a performance level extended to the same
 capacity

When the next performance level picks a subset of CPUs from the
previous one, gen_perf_pds_table() extends the previous level instead.
It inserts the extended level and then removes the old one by its
performance. When both have the same performance, the removal drops
the level that was just inserted.

This happens when the last two levels pick the same CPUs and so the
same performance, for example with CPUs offline or with identical CPUs
that have a single performance state. The top level with all the CPUs
is then lost, so some CPUs are left out of the CPU order.

Remove the old level before inserting the extended one.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Bastari Thamrin <thamrinjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/cpu_order.rs | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/cpu_order.rs b/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/cpu_order.rs
index 8e9ff381..49cce7fc 100644
--- a/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/cpu_order.rs
+++ b/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/cpu_order.rs
@@ -825,15 +825,18 @@ impl<'a> EnergyModelOptimizer<'a> {
                 }
             };
 
+            // Remove the old base before inserting its extension since both
+            // can have the same performance value and removing after
+            // inserting would drop the extension.
+            if let Some(del_pdsi) = del_pdsi {
+                self.perf_pdsi.borrow_mut().remove(&del_pdsi.performance);
+            }
+
             if let Some(best_pdsi) = best_pdsi {
                 self.perf_pdsi
                     .borrow_mut()
                     .insert(best_pdsi.performance, best_pdsi);
             }
-
-            if let Some(del_pdsi) = del_pdsi {
-                self.perf_pdsi.borrow_mut().remove(&del_pdsi.performance);
-            }
         }
 
         // Debug print of the generated table
